  "metadata": {
    "coordinateSpace": "Shared original GLB coordinates; +Y proximal, +X medial, +Z anterior; right limb.",
    "levels": "0=proximal,100=distal. GSV sampled Y84.7→7.5; SSV Y48→7.5. Not a full clinical acquisition route.",
    "method": "Each vessel anchor is the segment-length-weighted centroid of triangles intersecting a horizontal plane through the actual named vein mesh. Surface contact is the nearest skin-mesh ray intersection in the outward profile-gradient direction. Fallback projection uses the source skin ellipse profile when a regional skin mesh has no intersection.",
    "normal": "Outward skin-face normal at contact; profile-gradient normal for fallback. Unit vector in original GLB space.",
    "limitations": [
      "Atlas geometry and regional skin are not patient segmentation.",
      "Probe path models visual contact only; it does not model ultrasound beam, pressure, force or acoustic propagation.",
      "Interpolating sparse anchors is for visualization and can bridge local skin curvature; use small clearance at the probe face.",
      "GSV/SSV centre is an axial surface-section centroid, not a validated lumen centerline.",
      "SFJ is a source navigation landmark, not a universal anatomical location."
    ],
